Subject: [PATCH] stamp-p4: best-fit allocation for the NOMMU user pool (#51)

The vendor pool (0010/0070) keeps gen_pool's default first-fit, so
exec-sized blocks (0.5-1.8 MB) and small heap/stack allocs interleave in
the same regions: five SSH sessions push used to 97% with largest_free at
196 KB and alloc_fail climbing (#40, #49).

gen_pool_best_fit picks the smallest free block that holds each request,
leaving large contiguous spans available for the next exec image.  A/B
measurement lives in linux/tests/issue50-51-memory-2026-10-21.md.

---
diff --git a/mm/nommu_userspace_pool.c b/mm/nommu_userspace_pool.c
--- a/mm/nommu_userspace_pool.c
+++ b/mm/nommu_userspace_pool.c
@@ -88,6 +88,11 @@
 		pr_err("gen_pool_create failed\n");
 		return -ENOMEM;
 	}
+
+	/* #51: keep large free spans for exec images (default was
+	 * first-fit).  A/B numbers in linux/tests/. */
+	gen_pool_set_algo(user_pool, gen_pool_best_fit, NULL);
+	pr_info("user pool allocation algorithm: best-fit\n");
 
 	/*
 	 * Reserved-memory regions registered via RESERVEDMEM_OF_DECLARE
